eable on an already busy weekend.","evidence_claim":"The museum states that admission is always free and that photography is encouraged without flash, tripods, or selfie sticks.","source_url":"https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/your-visit.html","source_title":"Your Visit: Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Museum of Art","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Gallery hours are noon–5 p.m. Tuesday–Sunday, with noon–7 p.m. galleries during First Thursday events; closed Monday.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"showalter-fountain","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Showalter Fountain","title":"Pause at Showalter Fountain","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Fine Arts Plaza","notes":"Step outside after the galleries, circle the fountain for a wider view of the arts buildings, and use the plaza for a group photo.","short_summary":"An outdoor visual reset links several major arts destinations on Seventh Street.","evidence_claim":"IU’s official Fine Arts Plaza tour map places Showalter Fountain among the Eskenazi Museum of Art, IU Auditorium, and Lilly Library destinations.","source_url":"https://bloomington.iu.edu/campus-life/events/america-250/self-guided-tour.html","source_title":"Revolution and Reflection Self-Guided Tour","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor plaza feature; fountain operation may vary, and the cited page advises confirming each neighboring destination’s hours.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lilly-library","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Lilly Library","title":"Meet IU’s Special Collections","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Lilly Library","notes":"Enter during gallery hours, examine the current display labels, and ask staff how students can responsibly explore special collections later.","short_summary":"The first weekend gains a scholarly stop centered on rare books, manuscripts, and cultural records.","evidence_claim":"IU identifies the Lilly Library as its Bloomington rare-books, manuscripts, and special-collections library, with holdings across literature, history, science, media, and other fields.","source_url":"https://archives.iu.edu/repositories/lilly","source_title":"Lilly Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The current IU self-guided-tour page lists Monday–Thursday 9:30 a.m.–5:30 p.m., Friday 9:30 a.m.–5 p.m., Saturday 10 a.m.–4 p.m., and Sunday closure; confirm before visiting.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"iu-cinema","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Indiana University Cinema","title":"Check the IU Cinema Marquee","subtitle":"Saturday evening · IU Auditorium complex","notes":"Review the live program before heading over, reserve any required ticket, and arrive early enough to find the north-side entrance calmly.","short_summary":"A campus screening offers a structured evening activity without relying on age-restricted nightlife.","evidence_claim":"IU Cinema reports screenings four to five days per week during operating periods, usually at 7 p.m., and states that everyone is welcome.","source_url":"https://cinema.indiana.edu/plan-visit/index.html","source_title":"Plan Your Visit: Indiana University Cinema","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"IU Cinema closes on campus holidays and for several summer weeks. Screening times and ticket requirements vary, so consult the current program before going.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"cox-arboretum","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Jesse H. and Beulah Chanley Cox Arboretum","title":"Reset in the Cox Arboretum","subtitle":"Sunday morning · North-central campus","notes":"Take a quiet walk through the arboretum, choose a shaded place to sit, and compare upcoming schedules with your weekend companions.","short_summary":"A green-space stop creates an unhurried start before Sunday’s indoor destinations.","evidence_claim":"IU’s official first-year bucket list names studying in the Cox Arboretum as a campus experience for students.","source_url":"https://bloomington.iu.edu/admissions/orientation/steps/first-year/iu-bucket-list/","source_title":"IU bucket list","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor campus landscape; the cited page does not state hours, lighting conditions, or weather-related restrictions.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"herman-b-wells-library","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Herman B Wells Library","title":"Find Your Library Bearings","subtitle":"Sunday midday · Tenth Street and Eagleson Avenue","notes":"Locate the reference desk, quiet-study floors, and collaboration areas now so your first assignment does not become a navigation exercise.","short_summary":"A short building orientation turns the main library into a usable academic anchor.","evidence_claim":"IU identifies Wells Library as the Bloomington library-system hub, with humanities and social-sciences collections, research support, quiet study, and reservable collaboration rooms.","source_url":"https://libraries.indiana.edu/herman-b-wells-library","source_title":"Herman B Wells Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Hours change by date; IU Libraries’ current hours page should be checked before departure. Upper stacks close 30 minutes before the building.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"iu-museum-archaeology-anthropology","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Indiana University Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology","title":"Close with Material Culture","subtitle":"Sunday afternoon · 416 N. Indiana Avenue","notes":"Walk through the galleries with one question in mind: how do objects carry community histories? Record a few exhibits to revisit later.","short_summary":"The final stop broadens the weekend from campus navigation to human stories told through objects.","evidence_claim":"IUMAA states that it is free and open to all and presents collections connecting Indiana’s First Peoples, contemporary Hoosiers, and societies worldwide.","source_url":"https://iumaa.iu.edu/","source_title":"Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The museum currently lists Tuesday–Friday 10 a.m.–5:30 p.m., Saturday noon–5:30 p.m., and closure Sunday and Monday; move this stop to Saturday when those hours apply.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":["The sequence is intentionally flexible: IUMAA is currently closed Sundays, so its card explicitly directs visitors to move that stop to Saturday. IU Cinema programming and ticket prices vary by event.","Coordinates and maps URLs are null because exact values were not verified from the cited direct sources."]}],"warnings":[]}
